<subsection xml:id="subsubsec-linear-time-invariant-systems" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Linear Time-Invariant Systems</title>
  <idx>linear time-invariant systems</idx>
  <introduction>
    <p>
        Here, we introduce the fundamental ideas, terminology, and tools used to analyze one-dimensional signals in
        the time domain. Conceptual connections to the frequency domain, sampling, and basic transforms (e.g.,
        Laplace, Fourier, Z) will be briefly discussed to give the reader a sense of the broader scope of the study of
        signals and systems.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <!-- insert subsubsections here -->
  <xi:include href="def-dirac-delta.ptx"/>

 </subsection>